{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1098467-multiple-arcana-spells-2e-vs-1e","id":1098467,"title":"Multiple Arcana Spells: 2e vs 1e","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-30T10:21:33-07:00","id":1098467,"title":"Multiple Arcana Spells: 2e vs 1e","content":"Okay, I feel pretty comfortable with Mage, but there is something I still feel confused about<b></b>: spells with multiple arcana. Or at least, translating multiple arcana spells from 1e to 2e. Now, the full disclosure is that I'm solidly a 2e person. I do have a PDF of Mage 1e from DTRPG, but I have always found that book difficult to read, both from the density of the books content and from the physical layout, text colours and backgrounds used. As a result, there is a very high probability that I've missed something. I'm hoping that by talking myself through two examples I'll be able to clear things up. <br /> <br /> I'm going to start with Dialling the Lucky Number (Free Council) vs Lucky Number (2e Core). Their names and are a bit different, as are the mechanics but these are the same spell. Dialling the Lucky Number (1e) requires Fate ** + Space ** + Forces **, but Lucky Number requires just Fate **. Now, from Dave's blogs, I think that I understand this difference. In 1e, spells seem to have required every Arcana that could possibly be involved with the spell. Since the spell involved guessing someone's number (Fate) using a wired or wireless phone (Forces) over a long distance (Space), all three arcana were used. 2e revised the spell, decided that randomly dialling the correct number was the most important aspect of the spell was most important aspect of the spell, so now it's just Fate **. <br /> <br /> Even though I feel like I understand that spell, there are a number of 2e spells that throw me for a loop. For example, Bind Spirit (Spirit ****) allows you to add in Mind or Death to extend the effect to Goetia or Ghosts. There is no Bind Ghost or Bind Goetia spell listed, but I believe I am correct in my interpretation that Death **** or Mind **** should be able to create the Bind Ghost or Bind Goetia spells on their own without the addition of Spirit. If that is correct, could there also be a way of using just Forces or Space to replicate Dialling the Lucky Number? <br /> <br /> I think actually writing this out helped me with my thought process, so if I seem to have answered my own questions, that's why. Is my logic sound?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T10:33:01-07:00","id":1098471,"title":"","content":"I can't say for sure it's the intended interpretation, but it could be that the &quot;Add Death/Mind&quot; option is meant to allow someone to cast the same spell on more than one type of ephemeral entity without having to combine spells. A Bind Goetia spell would similarly have a &quot;Add Death/Spirit&quot; option.<br /> Forces and Space could not replicate Lucky Number as far as I know, but a Forces spell cast on two phones should be able to connect a call between them without having to get the number to the other phone. Only problem being is that you'd have to cast sympathetically on your target's phone in order to make real use of such a spell while Lucky Number grants you a piece of information without having to cast on the subject at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T10:44:03-07:00","id":1098475,"title":"","content":"The binding-and-banishing set does, in fact, exist in more than one ephemeral Subtle Arcana (it's Revenant/Exorcism in Death, and an equivalent effect can be extrapolated to exist for goetia after accounting for the more limited set of Manifestations available to Mind alone in the Invisible Entities rules) \u2014 the extra Arcana is mechanically there to remove the need to repurchase the same straightforward Rote or Praxis three different times.<br /> <br /> Forces and Space don't have effects within the technical purview of Lucky Number in the same way that &quot;Manifest or de-Manifest this ephemeral being&quot; does \u2014 some of the <i>outcomes</i> might be conceptually replicated, but control over distance or electricity/radio waves/etc isn't going to do anything to mess with the odds of blind success to a targeted end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T10:44:28-07:00","id":1098476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1098467-multiple-arcana-spells-2e-vs-1e?p=1098471#post1098471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't say for sure it's the intended interpretation, but it could be that the &quot;Add Death/Mind&quot; option is meant to allow someone to cast the same spell on more than one type of ephemeral entity without having to combine spells. A Bind Goetia spell would similarly have a &quot;Add Death/Spirit&quot; option.<br /> Forces and Space could not replicate Lucky Number as far as I know, but a Forces spell cast on two phones should be able to connect a call between them without having to get the number to the other phone. Only problem being is that you'd have to cast sympathetically on your target's phone in order to make real use of such a spell while Lucky Number grants you a piece of information without having to cast on the subject at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the way I'm leaning too.<br /> <br /> What you suggested actually does do what Dialing the Lucky Number does in 1e, since that spell was far more specific to telephone numbers (and therefore electricity) rather than 2e's Lucky Number, which works on any alphanumeric code, be it electronic or analogue. <br /> <br /> I guess part of where I'm going with this is converting spells from 1e to 2e. How do you recognize when a spell that required multiple arcana in 1e (Dialling the Luck Number) can be paired down to one arcana in 2e (Lucky Number)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T10:50:47-07:00","id":1098478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1098467-multiple-arcana-spells-2e-vs-1e?p=1098475#post1098475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The binding-and-banishing set does, in fact, exist in more than one ephemeral Subtle Arcana (it's Revenant/Exorcism in Death, and an equivalent effect can be extrapolated to exist for goetia after accounting for the more limited set of Manifestations available to Mind alone in the Invisible Entities rules) \u2014 the extra Arcana is mechanically there to remove the need to repurchase the same straightforward Rote or Praxis three different times.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gah! I missed it because I was searching for the spell under a different name. Thanks Satchel. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1098467-multiple-arcana-spells-2e-vs-1e?p=1098475#post1098475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forces and Space don't have effects within the technical purview of Lucky Number in the same way that &quot;Manifest or de-Manifest this ephemeral being&quot; does \u2014 some of the <i>outcomes</i> might be conceptually replicated, but control over distance or electricity/radio waves/etc isn't going to do anything to mess with the odds of blind success to a targeted end.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that makes sense and that's what I'm asking: can you get the same outcome as Lucky Number through different means of magic. If you had a way of knowing which phone you are targeting, you could call it without knowing the number using Forces, but you can't randomly guess it because that would take Fate magic. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T13:47:11-07:00","id":1098546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1098467-multiple-arcana-spells-2e-vs-1e?p=1098478#post1098478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that makes sense and that's what I'm asking: can you get the same outcome as Lucky Number through different means of magic. If you had a way of knowing which phone you are targeting, you could call it without knowing the number using Forces, but you can't randomly guess it because that would take Fate magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose if you had a sympathetic connection to the phone and employed the appropriate attainment, you could use Forces to 'call' it without knowing the number.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T14:05:34-07:00","id":1098557,"title":"","content":"Okay, so here is another one: Marked Power, from the Banishers book. Marked Power is Prime *** + Space **, allowing you to tamper with Tass so that you gain an intimate sympathetic connection to anyone who gains Mana from that tass as long as it remains in their system. Now, I know you could set a Hung Spell with a conditional trigger of eating the tass to create the sympathetic connection using Space, Time, and the Conditional Duration Fate attainment and achieve the same outcome. If you didn't want to hang the spell, could Marked with Power be cast with just Prime in 2e, just Space, or will it still require both arcana?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T15:24:41-07:00","id":1098581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1098467-multiple-arcana-spells-2e-vs-1e?p=1098557#post1098557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so here is another one: Marked Power, from the Banishers book. Marked Power is Prime *** + Space **, allowing you to tamper with Tass so that you gain an intimate sympathetic connection to anyone who gains Mana from that tass as long as it remains in their system. Now, I know you could set a Hung Spell with a conditional trigger of eating the tass to create the sympathetic connection using Space, Time, and the Conditional Duration Fate attainment and achieve the same outcome. If you didn't want to hang the spell, could Marked with Power be cast with just Prime in 2e, just Space, or will it still require both arcana?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Off the top of my head I would say it still requires both. Id see it something like a Prime spell to mark the Tass, and that would let you see when it was present in a pattern or a signature nimbus later or something. Adding Space would let you create a sympathetic connection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T15:28:19-07:00","id":1098583,"title":"","content":"Just use Space to create or gain a Sympathetic connection to the Tass, that will remain in place until that spell ends. It only lets you target the Tass though, not the person carrying or consuming it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T15:33:42-07:00","id":1098585,"title":"","content":"You could add an option to the already existing spell Web-Weaver:<br /> +1 Reach: Add Prime X (I think 1 or 2) and cast this spell on Tass. Once the Tass is consumed the sympathetic connection is transfered from the Tass to the person who consumed it.<br /> Edit: Though it seems to me it's pretty close to Dynamics, such as I've had that Practice explained to me. In that case it wouldn't be possible with Web-Weaver.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T15:48:18-07:00","id":1098591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1098467-multiple-arcana-spells-2e-vs-1e?p=1098583#post1098583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just use Space to create or gain a Sympathetic connection to the Tass, that will remain in place until that spell ends. It only lets you target the Tass though, not the person carrying or consuming it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point of Marked Power is to track the person who consumes the Tass, not the Tass itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T15:54:09-07:00","id":1098593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1098467-multiple-arcana-spells-2e-vs-1e?p=1098591#post1098591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point of Marked Power is to track the person who consumes the Tass, not the Tass itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, but if you want to do that you have to target the person, not the Tass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T15:57:20-07:00","id":1098595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1098467-multiple-arcana-spells-2e-vs-1e?p=1098593#post1098593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know, but if you want to do that you have to target the person, not the Tass.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How do you feel about my suggestion above? I'm not actually sure if the Prime altered Tass would still be traceable after it was absorbed as Mana into a Mage's Pattern, but that was the closest to replicate the spell and the desire of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> i could think of (in a few minutes without my book , at least).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T16:14:09-07:00","id":1098600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1098467-multiple-arcana-spells-2e-vs-1e?p=1098595#post1098595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you feel about my suggestion above? I'm not actually sure if the Prime altered Tass would still be traceable after it was absorbed as Mana into a Mage's Pattern, but that was the closest to replicate the spell and the desire of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> i could think of (in a few minutes without my book , at least).</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see the difference really, except adding an unnecessary step of marking the Tass/Mana. Prime could allow you to identify any Resonance that a point of Tass/Mana has, which would serve well enough as a marker, but Prime alone couldn't track its location. Space certainly can track the location of the Tass/Mana, but since the Sympathetic connection is to the Tass/Mana you can't target the person who possesses it or has it stored in their Pattern. On the bright side, if you've marked some Tass and managed to get a Mage to take it without noticing the marker they're likely to keep it on their person or in their Pattern. You could then use Correspondence to Sympathetically divine its current Sympathetic connections, being in contact with the person or in their Pattern should mean at least a Weak Sympathetic connection to that person. You could then use Borrow the Thread to take the Sympathetic connection between the Mana/Tass and the person carrying it or storing it in their Pattern which would -then- allow you to track that person Sympathetically. If they don't keep it on their person, then you've likely just gotten a tracker into their Tass cache or found someone that they're trying to pay off.<br /> <br /> Tl;dr You can't target someone via something they carry on or in their person, but you may be able to make useful inferences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T16:15:06-07:00","id":1098601,"title":"","content":"Seconding Elves of Zion and Tessie's ideas. The general trend with conjuctional Arcana seems to be first making an effect that works with one Arcana only, and then adding Arcana to it to expand the original effect. Like how fusing living beings and objects is handled by adding Life to Wonderful Machine, rather than being an entirely separate spell on its own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T16:19:20-07:00","id":1098603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1098467-multiple-arcana-spells-2e-vs-1e?p=1098600#post1098600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see the difference really, except adding an unnecessary step of marking the Tass/Mana. Prime could allow you to identify any Resonance that a point of Tass/Mana has, which would serve well enough as a marker, but Prime alone couldn't track its location. Space certainly can track the location of the Tass/Mana, but since the Sympathetic connection is to the Tass/Mana you can't target the person who possesses it or has it stored in their Pattern. On the bright side, if you've marked some Tass and managed to get a Mage to take it without noticing the marker they're likely to keep it on their person or in their Pattern. You could then use Correspondence to Sympathetically divine its current Sympathetic connections, being in contact with the person or in their Pattern should mean at least a Weak Sympathetic connection to that person. You could then use Borrow the Thread to take the Sympathetic connection between the Mana/Tass and the person carrying it or storing it in their Pattern which would -then- allow you to track that person Sympathetically. If they don't keep it on their person, then you've likely just gotten a tracker into their Tass cache or found someone that they're trying to pay off.<br /> <br /> Tl;dr You can't target someone via something they carry on or in their person, but you may be able to make useful inferences.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh yeah, I never meant that you would gain a sympathetic connection to Mage with the Mana at all. Just to the Tass\\Mana itself. My base spell would allow you to see when that Mana was used without a connection just looking at it with Mage Sight later. Or see it in the Pattern of the Mage when they were casting a spell and their Nimbus flared, that kind of thing. Otherwise I meant it as you said.<br /> <br /> My question before was about whether the Tass would remain a distinct 'thing' after be absorbed as Mana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T16:42:04-07:00","id":1098608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1098467-multiple-arcana-spells-2e-vs-1e?p=1098603#post1098603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah, I never meant that you would gain a sympathetic connection to Mage with the Mana at all. Just to the Tass\\Mana itself. My base spell would allow you to see when that Mana was used without a connection just looking at it with Mage Sight later. Or see it in the Pattern of the Mage when they were casting a spell and their Nimbus flared, that kind of thing. Otherwise I meant it as you said.<br /> <br /> My question before was about whether the Tass would remain a distinct 'thing' after be absorbed as Mana.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could probably cast a Knowing spell on a point of Tass such that you're aware of it regardless of your location, I imagine it would function a lot like Analyze Life and update you to state changes where Analyze Life would update you to condition of health.<br /> <br /> I would say though that Prime makes no distinction between Tass and Mana. Tass is just Mana bound in a stable form, storing Mana in your Pattern is basically the exact same thing. So if you saw a certain point of Tass/Mana once before, you can probably recognize it if you see it again even if it's been converted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T07:37:31-07:00","id":1098761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1098467-multiple-arcana-spells-2e-vs-1e?p=1098608#post1098608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You could probably cast a Knowing spell on a point of Tass such that you're aware of it regardless of your location, I imagine it would function a lot like Analyze Life and update you to state changes where Analyze Life would update you to condition of health.<br /> <br /> I would say though that Prime makes no distinction between Tass and Mana. Tass is just Mana bound in a stable form, storing Mana in your Pattern is basically the exact same thing. So if you saw a certain point of Tass/Mana once before, you can probably recognize it if you see it again even if it's been converted.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Works for me!<br /> <br /> How about you <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"